# AI tutor chat frontend conventions

## History payload to /api/chat

- The frontend keeps the FULL thread in `messages` for rendering, but
  sends only the last `MAX_PAYLOAD_TURNS = 24` items to the server.
- Each item must be `{ role: 'user' | 'model', parts: [{ text }] }`
  (Gemini-style). The legacy `{ role, content }` shape is not allowed
  in the API call.
- Hidden / system-trigger messages (`[trigger_greeting]`,
  `[REDIRECT_DIAGNOSTIC]`) MUST stay out of the payload. The user
  message you just appended is included unless `isHidden` is true.

## Agent switching

- Use `activeAgentId` everywhere. Do not concatenate it into URLs
  except via the existing `${API_URL}/api/history/${activeAgentId}`
  pattern.
- After switching agents, reset `dynamicChips` and scroll state so
  the previous agent's UI state does not bleed in.

## Streaming / suggestions parsing

- Replies may contain `[SUGGESTIONS: a, b, c]`, `[FORCE_TTS]`,
  `[TRIGGER_CLEAR]`, `[STUDENT_STATE: ...]`, `[REDIRECT_DIAGNOSTIC]`.
  Use `parseSuggestions` for chips and the existing regex blocks
  for the others. Do not introduce new tags without updating the
  backend tutor prompts AND `formatMessageContent`'s stripper.

## Don't

- Don't read or write `frontend/.env` from the agent's flow.
- Don't bypass `saveMessageToBackend` for messages you want
  persisted - the backend chat history is the source of truth on
  reload.
